@startuml UC-97 Remove Blog Post - Sequence Diagram (stereo)
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280

actor Moderator
participant ":BlogModerationPage" as UI <<user interaction>>
participant ":RemovePostDialog" as DIALOG <<user interaction>>
participant ":BlogController" as CTL <<coordinator>>
participant ":BlogPostService" as SVC <<business logic>>
participant ":BlogPostRepository" as POSTS <<interface>>
database DB

autonumber
Moderator ->> UI : Open a post of "My Subject Blogs" and click "Remove post"
activate UI
UI ->> DIALOG : Show the removal dialog requesting the removal reason
activate DIALOG

opt the reason is still empty or the moderator cancels the removal
  Moderator ->> DIALOG : Leave the reason field empty or click "Let me think again"
  DIALOG -->> Moderator : Keep the "Remove post" action disabled with MSG02 under the field, or close the dialog and leave the post published
end

Moderator ->> DIALOG : Enter the removal reason and click "Remove post"
DIALOG ->> UI : Report the confirmed removal with the entered reason
deactivate DIALOG
UI ->> UI : removePost()
UI ->> CTL : POST /api/blog-posts/{id}/removal
activate CTL
CTL ->> SVC : removeByModerator(id, reason)
activate SVC
SVC ->> POSTS : findPublishedById(id)
activate POSTS
POSTS ->> DB : SELECT * FROM blog_posts WHERE id = ? AND status = 'PUBLISHED'
activate DB
DB -->> POSTS : row / none
deactivate DB
POSTS -->> SVC : BlogPost
deactivate POSTS
SVC ->> SVC : require a non-empty reason and accept only a published post of the moderator assigned subject (BR-21)

alt the reason is empty, or the post is no longer published or belongs to another subject
  SVC -->> CTL : IllegalArgumentException / ResourceNotFoundException / ForbiddenOperationException
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 400 / 404 / 403
  UI -->> Moderator : Show MSG02 for the empty reason or the access-denied message, and refresh "My Subject Blogs" with the post unchanged
else the reason is entered and the post is published inside the assigned subject
  SVC ->> POSTS : save(post with status REMOVED_BY_MODERATOR, the reason and the removing moderator)
  activate POSTS
  POSTS ->> DB : UPDATE blog_posts SET status = 'REMOVED_BY_MODERATOR', removed_reason = ?, removed_by = ?, updated_at = ? WHERE id = ?
  activate DB
  DB -->> POSTS : Saved
  deactivate DB
  POSTS -->> SVC : BlogPost
  deactivate POSTS
  SVC ->> SVC : record the removal with its reason in the activity log and notify the author with the removal reason (see UC-93)
  SVC -->> CTL : void
  CTL -->> UI : HTTP 204 No Content
  UI ->> UI : loadPosts()
  UI -->> Moderator : Show MSG22 and refresh "My Subject Blogs" without the removed post and its discussion
end
deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
@enduml
